BloX v1.0.0 - Release Notes
Copyright (c) 2026 Sysop Network

Thank you for installing BloX, an ANSI falling-block puzzle game for
The Major BBS v10.

This is the initial public release.

What you get:
  * Classic 10 x 20 falling-block gameplay with the seven shapes
  * Modern 7-bag randomizer for fair piece distribution
  * Soft drop, hard drop, next-piece preview, ghost piece, pause
  * Level progression, combo and back-to-back bonuses
  * Persistent player statistics and achievements
  * An all-time Hall of Fame (Top 25, one entry per player)
  * Smooth, low-bandwidth ANSI rendering with differential updates

Getting started:
  1. Copy the package files into your BBS directory and start the
     server. BloX creates its data files on first run.
  2. Add a module page for "BloX" in the offline Menu Tree editor.
  3. Adjust options in the offline Configuration Editor if desired.

See README.TXT for full installation, configuration, and play details.

BloX is developed and maintained by Mark Laudenbach at Sysop Network.
